RESULT (:contract_version "1" :tool "read-file" :status "ok" :data (:path "/work/README.org" :snapshot "64aab1952b500be56d3c1d3d13105af32177839662627f2457811c4f6bd21a91" :total_lines 429 :offset 176 :column 1 :limit 7 :lines [(:number 176 :column 1 :text "- Parent bullets are sent explicitly under =# Parent Bullets= for Zen runs: each parent contributes its own body text, never its children, so nothing is duplicated and prior transcripts never leak into the payload." :partial :json-false) (:number 177 :column 1 :text "- Workspace selection is prose-first: a bullet like =look in ~/vault/projects/ogent for ideas= makes that directory the request workspace. Explicit labels (=Context:=, =Workspace:=, =Project:=, =Repo:=) still work, but are optional. The payload shows a =# Workspace= section, relative ogent tool paths resolve from that root, and code-grounded wording asks gptel to use read-only tools before answering." :partial :json-false) (:number 178 :column 1 :text "- Re-run a bullet from anywhere inside its transcript: =C-c . RET= appends a fresh run, =C-c . != (or =C-c C-c= on the transcript) replaces it. Earlier runs collapse automatically when a new run starts." :partial :json-false) (:number 179 :column 1 :text "- Press =C-c . q= to ask a new minibuffer question about the subtree at point." :partial :json-false) (:number 180 :column 1 :text "- Press =C-c . ?= when you are unsure: the ask menu names the active scope and offers run-current-bullet, re-run, inline ask, popup ask, malleable region ask/rewrite, edit application, context preview, and the full dispatcher." :partial :json-false) (:number 181 :column 1 :text "- Press =C-c . p= to open the dispatcher, pick models, and send the current subtree." :partial :json-false) (:number 182 :column 1 :text "- Doom/Evil users get the same command surface under =SPC o= when =ogent-setup-doom-bindings= or evil bindings are active." :partial :json-false)] :content "- Parent bullets are sent explicitly under =# Parent Bullets= for Zen runs: each parent contributes its own body text, never its children, so nothing is duplicated and prior transcripts never leak into the payload.
- Workspace selection is prose-first: a bullet like =look in ~/vault/projects/ogent for ideas= makes that directory the request workspace. Explicit labels (=Context:=, =Workspace:=, =Project:=, =Repo:=) still work, but are optional. The payload shows a =# Workspace= section, relative ogent tool paths resolve from that root, and code-grounded wording asks gptel to use read-only tools before answering.
- Re-run a bullet from anywhere inside its transcript: =C-c . RET= appends a fresh run, =C-c . != (or =C-c C-c= on the transcript) replaces it. Earlier runs collapse automatically when a new run starts.
- Press =C-c . q= to ask a new minibuffer question about the subtree at point.
- Press =C-c . ?= when you are unsure: the ask menu names the active scope and offers run-current-bullet, re-run, inline ask, popup ask, malleable region ask/rewrite, edit application, context preview, and the full dispatcher.
- Press =C-c . p= to open the dispatcher, pick models, and send the current subtree.
- Doom/Evil users get the same command surface under =SPC o= when =ogent-setup-doom-bindings= or evil bindings are active." :ends_with_newline t :has_more t :next_offset 183 :next_column 1) :error :json-null :next [(:tool "read-file" :args (:file_path "/work/README.org" :offset 183 :limit 7 :column 1) :snapshot "64aab1952b500be56d3c1d3d13105af32177839662627f2457811c4f6bd21a91" :call "(ogent-agent-call \"read-file\" '(:file_path \"/work/README.org\" :offset 183 :limit 7 :column 1))")])
